proposals.root_cause:
Two framings contradict. docs/fields.md armament[].range says 'Relative to the source's other weapons' (B-ra3 asks: this unit's weapons or the whole game's?). range-bands.json says 'relative to the top-down screen' and defines off-screen as 'beyond the camera view; needs spotting, a zoom or a scope mode'. Neither has a numeric anchor, unlike speed and price. Nothing covers:
- a weapon with a different reach per target (IFV: 150 against ground, 300 against air);
- maximum reach vs best distance (CoH carbine and BAR);
- a weapon with no figure (Terror Drone ray, IFV passenger results);
- what off-screen means for an RTS gun that outranges its own sight (Siege Tank: 13 against sight 11) or a shooter missile flown through its own camera.
